      "result": {
        "summary": "Southeast Asia is a prime destination for remote workers and digital nomads, offering a diverse range of cities and islands that cater to various lifestyles and budgets. Key attractions include affordable living, reliable internet, established co-working spaces, and thriving digital nomad communities, making it an ideal region for those seeking to combine work with travel.",
        "findings": [
          "Chiang Mai, Thailand, is recognized as a foundational digital nomad hub in Southeast Asia, celebrated for its affordability, high-speed internet, and a well-established community of remote professionals.",
          "Popular cities and regions for remote workers in Southeast Asia include Da Nang (Vietnam), Bali (Indonesia, especially Canggu), Bangkok (Thailand), Siem Reap (Cambodia), Koh Lanta and Koh Phangan (Thailand), Penang (Malaysia), Lombok (Indonesia, Kuta), Yogyakarta (Indonesia), Ho Chi Minh City (Vietnam), Singapore, and Phnom Penh (Cambodia).",
          "Many locations in Southeast Asia attract digital nomads due to factors such as affordable furnished accommodations, stable and fast Wi-Fi connectivity, readily available co-working spaces, and strong, supportive remote worker communities.",
          "While Singapore is a more expensive option, its advanced infrastructure, cleanliness, and rapid internet speeds draw higher-earning remote workers.",
          "The existing research provides sufficient information to identify popular cities for digital nomads in Southeast Asia, rendering additional specialist data collection unnecessary at this stage."
